cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NFE MXene Studio, please cite this software and the associated dataset."
title: "NFE MXene Studio"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ruck"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-30"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/lutengluo/Ruck-NFE-MXene-Studio"
abstract: >-
  An auditable forward-inverse materials-learning framework for nearly free
  electron states in MXenes. The software constructs physics-factorized
  pseudo-labels from converged VASP calculations, predicts calibrated NFE
  classes and auxiliary electronic observables with a periodic equivariant
  graph network, generates target-conditioned surface structures with flow
  matching, and applies topology, manifold, CHGNet, OOD, and duplicate gates
  before candidates enter a density-functional-theory validation queue.
keywords:
  - MXene
  - nearly free electron state
  - materials informatics
  - equivariant graph neural network
  - conditional flow matching
  - inverse materials design
  - density functional theory
  - CHGNet
